WEBVTT

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:03.126
Build a tool once and the request stops

00:00:03.187 --> 00:00:06.288
coming back to you: the job becomes a

00:00:06.378 --> 00:00:09.117
template other people fill in themselves,

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:12.144
correctly, without you in the loop.

00:00:12.938 --> 00:00:16.580
Your work is plain HTML, CSS and

00:00:16.638 --> 00:00:19.725
JavaScript - version-controlled, diffable,

00:00:19.783 --> 00:00:22.879
reviewable and running on an open engine,

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:25.936
so it stays yours with nothing to unwind

00:00:25.996 --> 00:00:27.119
later.

00:00:27.913 --> 00:00:30.494
Lolly is a platform-agnostic engine that

00:00:30.554 --> 00:00:33.003
runs the same render path across several

00:00:33.094 --> 00:00:36.230
shells - the web PWA, the desktop and

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:39.407
mobile apps, the CLI and the TUI - and

00:00:39.485 --> 00:00:43.018
tools are data rather than bundled code: a

00:00:43.079 --> 00:00:46.080
manifest, a template and optional hooks,

00:00:46.149 --> 00:00:49.645
so a new tool ships without an app update.

00:00:50.407 --> 00:00:53.248
Pick the lane below that matches what you

00:00:53.315 --> 00:00:55.268
are here to build.

00:00:56.063 --> 00:00:59.094
You are the multiplier in the relay: a

00:00:59.156 --> 00:01:01.929
creative authors the rules and you scale

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:05.604
them into a pipeline, a CLI batch or an

00:01:05.689 --> 00:01:09.077
MCP endpoint, so The lifecycle of a

00:01:09.139 --> 00:01:11.739
campaign follows one asset through all

00:01:11.834 --> 00:01:13.844
three pairs of hands.

00:01:14.644 --> 00:01:16.081
New here?

00:01:16.856 --> 00:01:19.704
The Quickstart gets a brand and your first

00:01:19.764 --> 00:01:22.769
render in place before you go deep.

00:01:23.541 --> 00:01:26.352
About names the licence boundary and the

00:01:26.413 --> 00:01:29.446
repositories each piece lives in, and

00:01:29.508 --> 00:01:32.246
Lolly for Operators is the door for

00:01:32.312 --> 00:01:34.924
whoever will ask you about rollout and

00:01:34.985 --> 00:01:36.444
security.

00:01:37.571 --> 00:01:38.988
Designers

00:01:39.919 --> 00:01:42.882
Bring finished work in, set the rules once

00:01:42.937 --> 00:01:45.920
and keep the tools you already use.

00:01:46.694 --> 00:01:49.646
What you decide here is what every tool in

00:01:49.687 --> 00:01:52.760
the gallery obeys, so a colour or a

00:01:52.824 --> 00:01:55.679
typeface is fixed in one place rather than

00:01:55.777 --> 00:01:58.094
argued about per asset.

00:01:58.881 --> 00:02:01.968
Import a design - bring a .

00:02:02.759 --> 00:02:03.724
fig, .

00:02:04.523 --> 00:02:05.695
penpot, .

00:02:06.505 --> 00:02:07.832
ai, .

00:02:08.604 --> 00:02:12.341
idml or SVG file in as an editable,

00:02:12.421 --> 00:02:14.902
re-renderable tool rather than a flat

00:02:14.962 --> 00:02:16.070
picture.

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:26.300
The Brand Studio - the on-device editor for logos, colours, type and the rest of the design system «#/start».

00:02:27.038 --> 00:02:31.092
Design Tokens - the DTCG token model a

00:02:31.154 --> 00:02:34.463
brand is expressed in and how a tool reads

00:02:34.524 --> 00:02:36.444
it at render time.

00:02:37.212 --> 00:02:40.180
Authoring Assets - catalog assets, tiers,

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:42.918
locales, palettes, themable icons and

00:02:43.007 --> 00:02:44.094
fonts.

00:02:44.869 --> 00:02:47.606
The Dashboard - your design system shown

00:02:47.688 --> 00:02:51.113
read-only, plus the capability map for the

00:02:51.175 --> 00:02:53.594
device in front of you.

00:02:54.719 --> 00:02:56.058
Developers

00:02:57.016 --> 00:03:00.240
One render path behind every surface: the

00:03:00.305 --> 00:03:03.484
GUI, the CLI and an agent all produce the

00:03:03.557 --> 00:03:06.395
same file from the same inputs.

00:03:07.157 --> 00:03:10.253
A tool is a manifest, a template and

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:13.066
optional hooks, and every input is

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:16.771
expressible as a URL parameter, which is

00:03:16.855 --> 00:03:19.932
why a link and a command line are the same

00:03:20.011 --> 00:03:21.269
thing here.

00:03:22.033 --> 00:03:24.767
Architecture - why Lolly exists, the

00:03:24.858 --> 00:03:28.300
engine/shell/tool separation and the

00:03:28.361 --> 00:03:30.945
commitments that hold it together.

00:03:31.706 --> 00:03:34.016
Authoring Tools - the full guide:

00:03:34.096 --> 00:03:36.685
manifest, template, styles, hooks,

00:03:36.746 --> 00:03:39.069
composition and publishing.

00:03:39.844 --> 00:03:43.773
Host API - the HostV1 capability bridge

00:03:43.869 --> 00:03:46.703
every tool is written against, plus the

00:03:46.765 --> 00:03:49.944
note that hooks are not a sandbox.

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:55.088
URL Mode - every input as a URL parameter:

00:03:55.152 --> 00:03:57.797
reserved params, compact encoding and

00:03:57.863 --> 00:03:59.269
packed links.

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:02.786
Constraints - why output comes out right

00:04:02.845 --> 00:04:05.577
by construction, with the tests that

00:04:05.632 --> 00:04:07.619
enforce each rule.

00:04:08.388 --> 00:04:12.058
Determinism - same inputs, same file: what

00:04:12.112 --> 00:04:15.444
is byte-reproducible and what is not.

00:04:16.217 --> 00:04:20.132
Reproducibility - the URL as the artifact,

00:04:20.192 --> 00:04:23.269
and how far a bare link can carry.

00:04:24.027 --> 00:04:26.476
CLI - headless rendering over the same

00:04:26.546 --> 00:04:30.519
path as the GUI, driven by --foo=bar argv

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:31.695
pairs.

00:04:32.488 --> 00:04:34.849
Signing from the terminal - give CLI

00:04:34.936 --> 00:04:38.656
output a real signing identity instead of

00:04:38.736 --> 00:04:41.294
an anonymous on-device key.

00:04:42.063 --> 00:04:45.100
TUI - the interactive terminal shell, for

00:04:45.161 --> 00:04:48.619
when a pipeline needs a human in it.

00:04:49.388 --> 00:04:53.227
MCP Server - the native endpoint an AI

00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:57.044
agent uses to discover and run tools.

00:04:57.812 --> 00:05:01.002
AI Agents - driving Lolly from a model,

00:05:01.061 --> 00:05:04.320
where a URL is the API.

00:05:05.069 --> 00:05:08.651
Browser Extension - capture a live URL as

00:05:08.738 --> 00:05:12.719
a reusable asset for a tool to compose.

00:05:13.476 --> 00:05:16.702
Content Credentials Identity - CA-issued

00:05:16.771 --> 00:05:20.199
signing for on-device C2PA, with the

00:05:20.272 --> 00:05:23.135
engine contracts behind what an export

00:05:23.195 --> 00:05:24.395
carries.

00:05:25.528 --> 00:05:26.985
Infrastructure

00:05:27.921 --> 00:05:30.895
A static host is the easy path and an

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:34.369
air-gapped install is the same install.

00:05:35.167 --> 00:05:38.262
Nothing in the render path needs a server,

00:05:38.341 --> 00:05:41.500
so what you are deploying is files, not a

00:05:41.594 --> 00:05:43.844
service to keep alive.

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:46.944
Deployment - the web app, the packaged

00:05:47.017 --> 00:05:49.916
apps and the two optional services: where

00:05:49.997 --> 00:05:51.770
each piece runs.

00:05:52.522 --> 00:05:55.682
Configuration - profiles, brand packs,

00:05:55.744 --> 00:05:58.289
capability gating, feature flags and

00:05:58.352 --> 00:06:00.370
catalog validation.

00:06:01.134 --> 00:06:03.896
Build Guide - build every target: CLI,

00:06:03.971 --> 00:06:08.069
TUI, desktop, mobile and the web PWA.

00:06:08.830 --> 00:06:12.049
Building for iOS - the extra gates Apple

00:06:12.137 --> 00:06:15.802
adds, and what a device build needs on top

00:06:15.837 --> 00:06:17.769
of the desktop one.

00:06:18.515 --> 00:06:20.824
Contributing Setup - a development

00:06:20.871 --> 00:06:24.049
checkout sized to what you are here to do,

00:06:24.131 --> 00:06:26.570
from a slim clone upward.

00:06:27.339 --> 00:06:30.419
Data Transfer - the lolly-backup bundle:

00:06:30.497 --> 00:06:33.080
envelope, integrity and the cross-shell

00:06:33.141 --> 00:06:34.619
guarantees.

00:06:35.398 --> 00:06:37.878
Threat Model & Trust Boundaries - what

00:06:37.944 --> 00:06:40.961
Lolly defends against, what it does not

00:06:41.023 --> 00:06:43.665
and where each boundary falls, before a

00:06:43.725 --> 00:06:45.269
review asks.
